A||||13||Mattyman||Fiero + Snow = What??||||5||
Z||000000||Mattyman||10-26-2001||11:23 PM||||As winter comes around and the snow begins to fall, well it already has been falling quite a bit here, I will have to drive my Fiero in the slick stuff. This will be the first time I will have to drive in in the snow.   I just wanted to get an idea of everyones opinion on how they do in snow.  I have gotten many different responses, like that they go good and others saying they are terrible.  So if anyone has experiece please let me know.  thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||10-26-2001||11:26 PM||||Fiero+Snow=Fun!<P>Hehe...anyway, it's not too bad once you get use to it. It's good to have skinny tires and a light foot. And never slam on the brakes! Unless of course you're in a huge empty parking lot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">              <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattyman||10-26-2001||11:29 PM||||Im looking forward to finding a nice open parking lot.  Im sick of trying to do donuts with an AWD astro van(with racing stripes, hahahaha) and a stupid RAV4.  Just hope I dont do any unexpected donuts in the middle of a highway or something.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-26-2001||11:42 PM||||Fiero + Snow = Snow Plow<P>Just watch the snow whiz by your window as you plow a path down the street. It is a real treat!!!<P>Contrary to popular belief, Fieros go fine in snow, it's stopping that is the trick!<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||California Kid||10-26-2001||11:48 PM||||No matter what anyone tells you, the only way you're going to learn how the car reacts, is to test it out in an empty snow covered parking lot. If you have anything like Eagle GT tires on there, replace with a narrower tire, or you're just asking for trouble in snow.  Too bad you have to drive it, snow/salt/ash/sand just isn't too good on any car, that stuff is only suited for cheap beater's, and lease cars.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||10-27-2001||12:00 AM||||Would it be OK to recommend SNOW tires? Not this M/S all-weather crap, it's your car, and your life, pony up the $200 for a set of brand new snow tires. <P>Pirelli has some good ones, Blizzaks rock, there are others...<P>Otherwise, the MR2s I've driven in snow were fine, with the drive wheels weighted by the drivetrain, the Fiero should be about the same. Ice and safety maneuvers would still not be fun, however. <BR><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||10-27-2001||01:18 AM||||I've always had good results with Fieros in snow. No, they aren't the best handling thing in snow, the understeer is exagerated even more when it gets slick outside. But, I have gone up steep hills in snow and passed FWD cars that couldn't make it up the same hill. <P>The car will only handle as well as the driver behind the wheel is my philosophy.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MikeSchaefer||10-27-2001||01:28 AM||||CIRCLES||||reg||6
Z||000008||Flamberge||10-27-2001||02:55 AM||||I cut my teeth on my first Fiero in Anchorage Alaska. I never once lost control, spun out, got in a wreck, got stuck, etc. <P>In Anchorage the first snows that "stick" are in October and it doesn't melt off until April during break up. Thus it will snow, get packed down on the roads, and then snow again on top of that, creating layer after layer of skating rink road surfaces. <P>The biggest problem I had was understeer (where you turn the wheel and the front end continues in a straight line) but it is easy to counteract by not going too fast and bey not turning the wheel more, because if you do, it will grab and you might spin out. But I agree 100% with the previous posts: practive in a big parking lot...doughnuts are a blast in a Fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR>- Flamberge<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://flamberge.iwarp.com/Serra3sm.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||10-27-2001||03:58 AM||||OK....... Heres my 0.02<P>I drove my Fiero all last winter.<P>Lowered 1 1/2"<BR>17" wheels (With rubberband tires)<P>+ The car is an Auto. I NEVER got stuck, & we had a lot of snow by me & they never plow. If that car will make it, I dont see why yours wont..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good Luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>-Haze<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">                 .                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> - Pennocks Wild Rides - <A HREF="http://clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000010||Ferrari_cdn||10-27-2001||05:00 AM||||My tires are P215/60.  Those would be bad on snow?<P>Anyway I did get a small taste of snow driving when we got a thin coat of snow (all melted now).  I did get quite a bit of understeer since I liked turning fast.  BUT, like common sense, don't give her a bit too much gas when turning in first or second, too easy to sway the back end out.  And once that ass starts swinging, it will want to keep swinging.  Catch it swinging before its too late and counter it, or you're in for a ride.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">  </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||1
Z||000011||Mach10||10-27-2001||05:18 AM||||Ferrari: I'm dropping down to a set of 195 studdlies... AND springing for the Calcious Traction Control System* (CTCS) That should keep me going<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>* == 50lb bag of kitty litter replacing Spare tire  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000012||Formula||10-27-2001||05:20 AM||||my biggest advice in a fiero on the snow...<P>GO SLOW!  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||85 gt fiero||10-27-2001||02:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mattyman:<BR><B>Just hope I dont do any unexpected donuts in the middle of a highway or something.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yah that would suck for you and your car. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES AND SOON TO BE BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
